public static void ReverseString(char[] str)
{
    int start = 0;
    int end = str.Length - 1;

    while (start < end)
    {
        // Swap characters at start and end indices
        char temp = str[start];
        str[start] = str[end];
        str[end] = temp;

        // Move the start and end indices towards the middle
        start++;
        end--;
    }
}
```

Explanation:
1. We initialize two pointers, `start` and `end`, which point to the first and last characters of the string, respectively.
2. We use a while loop to iterate until the `start` pointer becomes greater than or equal to the `end` pointer.
3. In each iteration, we swap the characters at the `start` and `end` indices.
4. After swapping, we increment the `start` pointer and decrement the `end` pointer to move them towards the middle of the string.
5. The loop continues until all characters have been swapped.
6. As the string is passed as a char array, we modify the input string in place without using any additional space.

